 ## Background
-SDF transformations originated in the context of ray marching and implicit surface rendering. Early work by Hart [S6] formalized the use of inverse transformations for isometries and uniform scaling. Barr [S7] extended this to general deformations (taper, twist) and introduced the concept of Lipschitz constants to ensure the validity of the sphere tracing algorithm. The technique became popular in shader programming and procedural modeling (e.g., "shadertoy" culture) for its ability to create complex, animated geometry with minimal code [S1, S4, S5, S8].
